# Normalise line endings for every contributor, regardless of platform.
#
# Why this file exists: `.prettierrc` sets `endOfLine: "lf"`, but Git on
# Windows ships with `core.autocrlf=true` by default. Without an override, a
# Windows checkout rewrites every text file to CRLF, so `npm run format:check`
# fails on ~all files locally while passing on Linux CI. Declaring `eol=lf`
# here makes the checkout deterministic everywhere and keeps the Prettier gate
# meaningful on all platforms.
#
# `text=auto` also lets Git detect binaries on its own, so the explicit
# `binary` rules below exist only to be unambiguous about assets we never want
# touched by any normalisation.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# Owned by the package manager; leave byte-for-byte as npm writes it.
package-lock.json -text
